     "design": {
      "purpose": "Solve equal-groups and array problems with multiplication and division within 100.",
      "principles": [
       "PRINCIPLE_INTERLEAVING"
      ],
      "rationale": "The unknown is sometimes the total, sometimes the size of each group and sometimes the number of groups, which are the three equal-groups problem types in 3.OA.A.3. Students who draw the groups or an array can check the operation they chose.",
      "misconceptions": [
       "Multiplying whenever two numbers appear.",
       "Treating the number of groups and the size of each group as the same kind of number, so 42 ÷ 7 and 42 ÷ 6 look the same."
      ],
      "references": [
       "Common Core Standards Writing Team (2011), Progressions for the Common Core State Standards in Mathematics, K, Counting and Cardinality; K-5, Operations and Algebraic Thinking"
